  "reason": "The records point toward the result but do not disclose the decisive combination. R2, R4, and R18 establish that pressure, including pressure combined with temperature, can drive structural transformations in HEAs, while R7 shows that the same AlCoCrFeNi system can be strongly reorganized by coupled thermal and mechanical processing. R3 and R12 provide particularly strong support for the proposed mediator and mechanism: coherent interfaces can transmit dislocations, relieve stress concentrations, and suppress microcracking or cleavage. R1, R8, and R13 supply the relevant FCC/B2 eutectic-lamellar background, and R5, R10, R14, and R16 support synergistic plasticity from faults, twins, dislocations, and transformations. Nevertheless, none of the records applies static HPHT treatment in a hexahedron-anvil apparatus to the target eutectic alloy or suggests that it will convert its incoherent FCC/B2 lamellae into a hierarchical coherent-interface pattern. Selecting that specific intervention to produce that specific architecture would therefore require a substantial new idea."
